# SHA-256 of the native libraries that are linked into Talia but are NOT in git
# (they are built locally by native/build-bitboxffi.sh and
# native/build-bdkwallet.sh).
# scripts/ios-archive.sh refuses an App Store / TestFlight archive whose libraries
# differ from these lines, so the Bitcoin core inside a store build is tied to a
# commit. native/bitboxffi/lib and native/bdkwallet/lib may hold ONLY the files
# listed here (they are on the linker's search path), so the simulator
# libraries the build scripts also write are pinned too.
# Pinned 2026-10-01 from the libraries App Store build 20 was archived
# with; the -sim.a lines added 2026-10-02 from the same build of each library.
# The old engine's removal (decided 2026-11-04) took bdkffi (bdk-ffi 0.30,
# the old engine) with its record and pins. The bdkwallet record below still
# names its files in two "# gated" lines: that build's overlap gate judged
# them, and the record is the build's own (archive-provenance.js
# RETIRED_NATIVE_LIBS sets them aside).
#
# Each library's "# source" line (decided 2026-09-26) names the 21st Capital
# repo and the full commit its pinned files were built from, and its "# built"
# lines the digest of every file that build wrote. The build script writes
# them itself, after building from a clean checkout whose HEAD it found on
# that repo (scripts/native-sources.js). scripts/ios-archive.sh refuses, with
# no override, an archive when a line is missing or malformed or names any
# other repo, when a library's pins are not exactly the files its recorded
# build wrote, or when a library on disk is not the pinned one; it copies the
# record into the archive's provenance.
# After a rebuild: test the libraries on the phone (scripts/ios-device.sh
# takes the recorded build before it is pinned; an archive never does), then
# pin them with
#   node scripts/native-sources.js pin <bitboxffi|bdkwallet>
# (it pins only the files the recorded build wrote; never edit a digest by
# hand) and commit the record and the pins TOGETHER. To keep the old libraries
# instead, put back this file AND the old files.
# Every pinned file has a byte-identical copy, named <sha256>-<file name>, in
# a talia-native-libs-<date> release of the private bdk-ffi-fork repo (since
# 2026-10-22): upload a new pin's copies to a new release, add its tag to
# COPIES.tags in scripts/native-sources.js, check them with
#   node scripts/native-sources.js copies
# and a checkout without the libraries gets them back, checked against these
# pins and then verified, with
#   node scripts/native-sources.js restore <bitboxffi|bdkwallet|all>
# (bdkffi's copies stay in their releases: after reverting the removal
# commit, restore bdkffi puts its pinned files back)

